      "card_ids": ["C30"]
    },
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "not_applicable",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C24"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "The query has no reported external condition, while several high-F records come from cirrhosis where first-pass elimination is reduced; exact healthy-state F may be lower, though normal pethidine F (~48%) and other non-cirrhosis records remain above 20%.",
    "Meptazinol controls may have F below 20%, but this context is structurally less close and is not used as a primary basis for the query.",
    "No experimental solubility, permeability, or first-pass metabolism data are available for the query.",
    "The FK788 rat value of 9.6% is species-specific and not transferable to the human-oriented query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L2 context records largely corroborate the L1 positive outcomes for the closest structural contexts (pethidine, encainide, tenidap) and do not provide transferable affirmative evidence for F < 20%. The meptazinol cirrhosis context is weakened by the control comparison, and the FK788 rat value is not applicable. The prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

